# Dredge 6 (CR 702.52a): "As long as you have at least N cards in your library, if you would draw a card, you may instead mill N
# cards and return this card from your graveyard to your hand" - a static ability of the card in the graveyard, and dredge
# "can replace any card draw", the draw step's too (its rulings). Bot1 makes itself discard Golgari Grave-Troll with
# Thoughtseize on turn 1. Its turn 3 draw for the turn is replaced: Bot1 is asked, dredges, and mills six cards, and the Troll
# comes back to its hand; it draws no card. On turn 5 the Troll is in hand, not in the graveyard, so nothing replaces the draw.

[Bot1 Deck]
Swamp
Thoughtseize
Golgari Grave-Troll
